# interplay_limits_children_suspend: All 63 child FIFOs (maxFIFOCount 64 at version 245), each carrying an exec for a task of its own (tasks 1-63 over one shared space, each filling its own byte), gated on the root. At most 32 of them may wait at once: DeviceCore::add_wait marks a waiter with a 32-bit `1 << waiter`, so child k and child k + 32 share a bit and asserting that the bit is clear kills the host (interplay_limits_child_wait_alias_dies). So children 1-31 wait on the root while it presents a frame on port 0, then open; then children 32-63 wait (32 waiters, child 32 on bit 0) and open; their block calls, from many threads, sorted. Round 1: children 32-63 are rung gated again, and the host suspends while they wait: rvg_device_finish_suspend abandons the 32 waits, and the fresh device re-creates 63 children and 63 tasks (under isolation, 63 new service instances) from the root page; the 32 parse their rings again and wait again. The root presents the other frame and opens the gate; then children 1-31 run round 1. The page holds both rounds.
